text","text":"The shared-cache `:memory:` URI is shared across the whole process — so multiple `create_app(\":memory:\")` calls in the same process share the same DB. The `test_full_crud_lifecycle` test created books, and they leak into `test_list_empty`. I need per-app isolation.\n\nThe cleanest fix: give each in-memory DB a unique name. Use a random URI name per app instance. Let me use `uuid` to make the memory DB name unique.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_058d7902e0019pGsRX1rg2wMom","sessionID":"ses_fa72b1d29ffe24CcENoHmfOP3D","messageID":"msg_058d77978001JZYKdsvyy12YV2"}}
